<?xml version="1.0" encoding="utf-8"?><!--
    Level rewards, built on the LevelRewards.dc.html handoff and painted in
    this app's palette (see the Wallet block in colors.xml for the mapping).

    Four departures from the handoff, all because of what this economy
    actually does rather than preference:

      * No "Claim reward" button, and no "N to claim" badge. Milestone stars
        are paid by awardReward inside the same transaction that crosses the
        level - there is nothing left for a button to do, and one that only
        looked like it worked would be worse than none.
      * No level NAMES ("Rookie", "Mythic"). Levels here are numbers on a
        curve; there is no name table to read one from.
      * Thresholds are XP, not "lifetime points". Points are spent at
        cashout; XP is what the curve is built on.
      * Only levels that unlock something are listed. Every level from 2 up
        pays stars, so in practice that is the whole climb; level 1 is absent
        because accounts are CREATED there and it is never crossed, so a rung
        for it could never pay. The note under the section heading counts what
        is listed against the curve's top level, which is what shows when a
        level has been emptied in the console.

    THE WHOLE SCREEN IS THE LIST. The chrome that used to sit above and below
    the rungs is now view_level_rewards_header and view_level_rewards_footer,
    concatenated around the rungs by a ConcatAdapter.

    That is not decoration - it is the only arrangement that recycles. A
    RecyclerView inside the NestedScrollView this replaces would be measured
    unbounded and would lay out all thirty rungs on open, which is exactly
    the cost the adapter exists to avoid.

    Padding moved here from the LinearLayout it replaces, with
    clipToPadding="false" so the top and bottom insets stay scrollable
    spacing rather than clipping the rows.

    The bottom nav is the activity's PixelBottomNav, not redrawn here.
-->
<androidx.recyclerview.widget.RecyclerView xmlns:android="http://schemas.android.com/apk/res/android"
    xmlns:tools="http://schemas.android.com/tools"
    android:id="@+id/levelRewardsList"
    android:layout_width="match_parent"
    android:layout_height="match_parent"
    android:background="@color/background_dark"
    android:clipToPadding="false"
    android:paddingStart="17dp"
    android:paddingTop="12dp"
    android:paddingEnd="17dp"
    android:paddingBottom="24dp"
    android:scrollbars="none"
    tools:listitem="@layout/item_level_rung" />
